WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.029
Who would have thought that water in a can
would become the second-best-selling drink

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:06.029
on Amazon?

00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:08.090
And not only there.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:13.750
Liquid Death is believed to be the fastest-growing
non-alcoholic beverage of all time.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.820
It sold its first can in 2019 and raked in
$3 million in revenue that year.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.590
In 2022, the company’s revenue soared to
$130 million.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:27.330
And is currently valued at $700 million.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.210
CEO Mike Cessario recognized that many people
were looking for a more environmentally-friendly

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.380
alternative to plastic water bottles.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.320
What is Liquid Death, are these kids drinkin’?

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:42.520
By packaging water in a can of what looks
like craft beer, Liquid Death created a unique

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.520
identity.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.340
But it wasn't just the packaging that made
Liquid Death cool.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.790
It’s the wicked marketing.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:53.879
For years a bunch of marketing f*?^ boys have
tricked you into thinking water is some girly

00:00:53.879 --> 00:00:55.989
drinks for Yoga moms.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:01:01.129
Well, hold onto your high heels.

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:04.549
Because I’ve got news.

00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:07.120
Water isn’t cute.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.520
Water is deadly.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:15.840
Their ads are funny and satirical, drawing
people to the brand’s edgy personality.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.090
Water is liquid death.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:23.360
One of the top comments on this video is:
“I don't mind commercials when they are

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.570
as entertaining as this”

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:30.220
Mike told the non-profit news organization
Marketplace: “If you can make people laugh,

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:35.009
they will have a deeper connection with your
brand, regardless of the functional differences

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:36.650
of your liquid.”

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:40.220
Big companies think they set themselves apart
because of unique ingredients.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:43.310
But those can be replicated easily.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:48.250
Strong brands mean more to people than the
product itself.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:53.250
So the CEO of Liquid Death is admitting it’s
not even about the taste of the drink!

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.590
Not the worst water I’ve ever tasted.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:02:00.060
Mike thinks of his beverage startup as being
like Saturday Night Live, with comedians writing

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.130
the skits.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:06.060
For years, he worked on marketing campaigns,
including for the dairy brand Organic Valley,

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:09.660
which produced this hilarious commercial about
their protein shake.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:15.290
Just tell a bro it has a tonne of protein,
and he’ll pound the s*&amp;^ out of it.

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:17.980
That sense of humor is written all over the
cans.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:22.410
The blurb on the side reads: “When a group
of teenagers set off into the mountains for

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:27.650
a weekend of drinking regular water in plastic
bottles, they became hunted by an aluminum

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:33.080
can of mountain water that was dead set on
murdering their thirsts and recycling their

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.080
souls,”

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:39.560
The can draws inspiration from the kind of
artwork on popular energy drinks.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:44.400
Mike got the idea for Liquid Death while attending
the Vans Warped Tour which was sponsored by

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:49.420
the energy drink Monster.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.370
He noticed that band members didn’t want
to consume energy drinks for health reasons.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:58.520
So, Monster gave them cans filled with water
so they could still promote the brand.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:02.000
These cans of Monster tour water were not
for sale to the public.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.370
Mike thought to himself: Why not sell water
in a can and market it in the same fun and

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.380
rebellious way as energy drinks or beer?

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:16.200
And, it just so happens that alcohol consumption
appears to be on the decline for young people.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:21.540
Among American adults, Gallup showed that
those aged 18 to 34 are less likely to drink

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.879
alcohol than those aged 35 to 54.

00:03:24.879 --> 00:03:34.659
A large UK study in 2019 showed 26% of young
people in England are not drinking at all.

00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:40.390
Liquid Death says a quarter of its consumers
are Gen Zers, between 18 to 25 years old.

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:45.349
Its TikTok account is the second most followed
of any beverage brand that I could find, after

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:46.750
Red Bull.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:51.689
Even though some investors thought it was
a dumb idea, Mike knew he was onto something.

00:03:51.689 --> 00:03:57.319
The company created buzz on social media even
before launching the product just to see its

00:03:57.319 --> 00:03:58.319
potential.

00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:03.709
Without even having a real product, we had
more social followers than Aquafina.

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:07.860
Look how many people are messaging us asking
how they can get this.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:11.530
Look how many people are sharing an image
of a beverage product.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:16.959
Like, who shares an image of a beverage and
how often on social media?

00:04:16.959 --> 00:04:17.959
Not too often.

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:22.729
Their fans are so loyal that they’re getting
the brand permanently etched on their skin.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:27.960
The company says they know of at least 300
people with Liquid Death tattoos.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:33.310
Liquid Death has also built brand loyalty
through unusual celebrity endorsements.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:38.720
Like releasing a limited edition line of Tony
Hawk skateboards infused with his blood.

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:41.490
And they’re gonna use it for skateboard
graphics?

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:45.090
The idea was so provocative that several news
outlets covered it.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.430
Resulting in free publicity.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:51.880
Liquid Death has expanded its lineup from
selling mountain water and sparkling to include

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:56.760
flavored water and ice teas with witty names
that are a play on phrases:

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:01.110
Convicted Melon - Convicted Felon
Grim Leafer - Grim Reaper

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.840
Rest in Peach - Rest in Peace

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.770
Liquid Death is a masterclass in the art of
marketing.

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:13.130
It has struck the right balance by being provocative
enough to stand out while not crossing the

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:15.330
line into offensiveness.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:20.510
Liquid Death’s goal is to become a multi-billion-dollar
beverage company like Red Bull.

